  "body": {
    "id": "prop:finite-star-dictionary",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "For every \\(C,D\\in\\mathfrak S_p\\), if \\(\\mathsf S(C)\\neq\\mathsf S(D)\\), then \\(\\mathcal W_2(C)\\not\\subseteq\\mathcal M(D)\\) or \\(\\mathcal W_2(D)\\not\\subseteq\\mathcal M(C)\\). Moreover, \\[|\\mathcal W_2(E_0)|\\leq\\sum_{j\\in V}\\left(|\\Pi^{E_0}_j|+\\binom{|\\Pi^{E_0}_j|}{2}\\right)\\leq\\frac{p^2(p-1)}{2}.\\]",
    "free_symbols": [
      "C",
      "D",
      "Estate",
      "StateClass",
      "Sig",
      "W2",
      "Model",
      "PiE",
      "V",
      "p"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:binary-star-library",
      "thm:bounded-binary-star-separation"
    ],
    "justification": "The pointwise router induces a finite universal test dictionary whose size is explicit before any data are observed.",
    "gap": "BoegeKubjasMisraSolus2026 decides equality using rational model constraints, whereas this result reduces inequality detection on the blocked class to finitely many binary stars.",
    "consumer": "Exact-arithmetic regression tests can precompute the complete separating library for small or moderate labelled systems.",
    "proof_tex": "If \\(\\mathsf S(C)\\ne\\mathsf S(D)\\), then \\(\\texttt{thm:bounded-binary-star-separation}\\) returns a source \\(E\\in\\{C,D\\}\\) and a separating covariance activating one or two blocks at one target.  By \\(\\texttt{def:binary-star-library}\\), it lies in \\(\\mathcal W_2(E)\\) and not in the other model.  Hence\n\\[\n \\mathcal W_2(C)\\not\\subseteq\\mathcal M(D)\n \\quad\\text{or}\\quad\n \\mathcal W_2(D)\\not\\subseteq\\mathcal M(C).\n\\]\nFor \\(b_j=|\\Pi^{E_0}_j|\\), target \\(j\\) offers \\(b_j+\\binom{b_j}{2}\\) choices.  Duplicate covariances only reduce the cardinality.  Since \\(b_j\\le|\\operatorname{pa}_{G_{E_0}}(j)|\\le p-1\\),\n\\[\n |\\mathcal W_2(E_0)|\n \\le\\sum_{j\\in V}\\frac{b_j(b_j+1)}2\n \\le p\\frac{(p-1)p}{2}.\n\\]\nEmpty parent sets contribute zero.",
